    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.95,
      "end_seconds": 293.91,
      "duration_seconds": 15.96,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, it fits best with a reactive lymph node after a throat infection. It could also be something that needs a tissue diagnosis, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.52,
      "end_seconds": 339.8,
      "duration_seconds": 27.28,
      "text": "we should do blood tests for neck lump. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. We should do an ultrasound of the neck for neck lump. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Check the lump once a week and let me know if it grows or becomes hard"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.77,
      "end_seconds": 357.08,
      "duration_seconds": 16.31,
      "text": "Try to get to bed and wake up at the the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. We'll catch up in three weeks. How would you describe the plan, so we're on the same page?"
    },
